  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "In the avatar descriptor, under Playable Layers > Special I'd like to have a controller for setting the pose of the avatar in the avatar selection menu preview (the slowly rotating one).\nYou can currently accomplish this by using the default state of the locomotion layer, but there are limitations--nothing will run (constraints, etc) and, while you can pose non-humanoid bone transforms, it's easy to mess up the avatar in such a way that will break locomotion. It's also impossible to blend out locomotion layers. By having this pose in a separate controller, the avatar would have a fresh, distinct locomotion layer when actually loaded, so pose manipulations for the menu would never break anything.",
